    "markdown": "![Hugging Face's logo](https://huggingface.co/front/assets/huggingface_logo-noborder.svg) Hugging Face⟨1⟩\n  *  Models ⟨2⟩\n  *  Datasets ⟨3⟩\n  *  Spaces ⟨4⟩\n  *  Buckets new⟨5⟩\n  *  Docs ⟨6⟩\n  *  Enterprise ⟨7⟩\n  * Pricing⟨8⟩\n  *     * Website\n      *  Tasks⟨9⟩\n      *  HuggingChat⟨10⟩\n      *  Collections⟨11⟩\n      *  Languages⟨12⟩\n      *  Organizations⟨13⟩\n    * Community\n      *  Blog⟨14⟩\n      *  Posts⟨15⟩\n      *  Daily Papers⟨16⟩\n      *  Hardware⟨17⟩\n      *  Learn⟨18⟩\n      *  Discord⟨19⟩\n      *  Forum⟨20⟩\n      *  GitHub⟨21⟩\n    * Solutions\n      *  Team & Enterprise⟨7⟩\n      *  Hugging Face PRO⟨22⟩\n      *  Enterprise Support⟨23⟩\n      *  Inference Providers⟨24⟩\n      *  Inference Endpoints⟨25⟩\n      *  Storage Buckets⟨5⟩\n  * * * *\n  * Log In⟨26⟩\n  * Sign Up⟨27⟩\n\n\n#   Datasets:⟨3⟩\n* * *\n ![](https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/67cef22278bb578b4c7331ed/lhFL7HECM_n0YbIVUXAT-.png) ⟨28⟩\nHaeryz⟨28⟩\n/\nputusan-structured-extraction⟨29⟩\nlike 0\nTasks:  Text Generation ⟨30⟩\nModalities:  Tabular ⟨31⟩ Text ⟨32⟩\nFormats:  parquet ⟨33⟩\nLanguages:  Indonesian ⟨34⟩\nSize:  10K - 100K ⟨35⟩\nTags:  legal ⟨36⟩ indonesian ⟨37⟩ court-decisions ⟨38⟩ structured-extraction ⟨39⟩\nLibraries:  Datasets ⟨40⟩ pandas ⟨41⟩ Polars ⟨42⟩ + 1\nLicense:\ncc-by-4.0\n Dataset card ⟨29⟩ Data Studio ⟨43⟩ Files Files and versions xet ⟨44⟩ Community 1 ⟨45⟩\nDataset Viewer\n Auto-converted to Parquet⟨46⟩ API Embed  Duplicate⟨47⟩ Data Studio\nSubset (4)\nsft · 3.08k rows\nsft (3.08k rows) grpo (667 rows) rag (665 rows) sft_sections (18.4k rows)\nSplit (3)\ntrain · 2.47k rows\ntrain (2.47k rows) validation (311 rows) test (296 rows)\nSQL\nConsole\nThe dataset viewer is not available for this split.\nParquet error: Scan size limit exceeded: attempted to read 475133243 bytes, limit is 300000000 bytes Make sure that 1. the Parquet files contain a page index to enable random access without loading entire row groups2. otherwise use smaller row-group sizes when serializing the Parquet files \n\n```\nError code:   TooBigContentError\n\n```\n\nNeed help to make the dataset viewer work? Make sure to review how to configure the dataset viewer⟨48⟩, and open a discussion⟨49⟩ for direct support.\n  * Files⟨50⟩\n  * Schema (uniform across all files)⟨51⟩\n  * Row counts⟨52⟩\n  * `sft_sections` config (per-section SFT)⟨53⟩\n\n\n#   ⟨54⟩ Putusan structured-extraction dataset \nBuilt 2026-07-08T23:02:28+00:00 by `notebooks/build_dataset.py` (seed 3407).\nIndonesian court-decision (putusan) extractive-structuring dataset over three corpora (Anak, Asusila, TPPO). Each row is one model extraction of one source document into 31 canonical sections of verbatim spans. Empty sections were completed from sibling model extractions of the same document where available (`cross_model_fill_json` records per-section donor provenance).\n##   ⟨50⟩ Files \n`{sft,grpo,rag}/{train,val,test}.parquet` — purposes are document-disjoint (SFT 70% / GRPO 15% / RAG 15% of unique documents per corpus), then each purpose is split train 80% / val 10% / test 10%. All rows of a document (one per annotator model) share the same purpose+split, so there is zero document leakage across any pair of files.\n##   ⟨51⟩ Schema (uniform across all files)   \n| column  | type  | description  |  \n| --- | --- | --- |  \n| id  | str  | `corpus/annotator_model/sha16`  |  \n| corpus  | str  | Anak, Asusila, or TPPO  |  \n| annotator_model  | str  | model that produced the extraction (GPT/Deepseek/Qwen)  |  \n| source_file / source_sha256  | str  | source decision text identity  |  \n| extraction_method  | str  | extraction protocol tag  |  \n| purpose / split  | str  | sft-grpo-rag / train-val-test  |  \n| split_seed  | int  | RNG seed used for the deterministic split  |  \n| input_text  | str  | decision body reconstructed from section spans  |  \n| target_json  | str  | full 31-key supervision target (JSON)  |  \n| sections_json  | str  | the 31 sections alone (JSON)  |  \n| messages  | list<struct{role,content}>  | system/user/assistant conversation (SFT)  |  \n| prompt  | list<struct{role,content}>  | system+user only (GRPO rollout prompt)  |  \n| answer  | str  | reference answer for reward computation (GRPO)  |  \n| n_nonempty_sections / n_empty_sections / empty_sections  | int/list  | section coverage  |  \n| cross_model_fill_json  | str  | {section: donor_model} completion provenance  |  \n| n_sections_filled_cross_model  | int  | sections completed from a sibling model  |  \n| models_covering_doc  | list  | all models that extracted this document  |  \n| n_input_chars / n_input_words / n_target_chars  | int  | size statistics  |  \n##   ⟨52⟩ Row counts   \n| purpose  | train  | val  | test  |  \n| --- | --- | --- | --- |  \n| sft  | 2468  | 311  | 296  |  \n| grpo  | 534  | 68  | 65  |  \n| rag  | 529  | 68  | 68  |  \nTotal rows: 4407 (expected 4500; shortfall is missing/failed extractions — see `dataset_info.json` `per_dir_file_counts`).\n##   ⟨53⟩ `sft_sections` config (per-section SFT) \nDerived from the `sft` config by `notebooks/build_sections_dataset.py` — same documents, same document-disjoint splits, zero leakage. Each parent document becomes SIX examples that keep the FULL reconstructed body as input but ask for only 1-2 sections (matching inference, where a user uploads a whole decision and asks for one or two sections). The 31-key `sft` config is unchanged.\nSection sampling is deterministic and difficulty-weighted (measured on `sft/train.parquet`): `ahli` (67% empty) is asked for every document; `penangkapan`/`surat` (29%/16% empty) alternate; two of the five long-body sections (`pertimbangan_hukum`, `saksi`, `dakwaan`, `terdakwa`, `fakta_hukum`) rotate; one medium section (`tuntutan`, `penahanan`, `petunjuk_barang_bukti`, `amar_putusan`) rotates; and one PAIR of the 19 trivial identity/date sections rotates (this is the two-section example). ~16% of examples ask for a section that is empty in that document, so the model learns to answer with an empty list.\nExtra/changed columns vs the parent schema: `parent_id` (the `sft` row id), `requested_sections` (list), `n_requested`, `n_empty_requested`; `target_json`/`answer` contain only `{\"sections\": {...}, \"empty_sections\": [...]}` for the requested keys; the system prompt names the requested sections. Columns about the full 31-section extraction (`sections_json`, `cross_model_fill_json`, etc.) are omitted. 7 exact-duplicate parent train rows (same sha under two filenames) are dropped.  \n| sft_sections  | train  | val  | test  |  \n| --- | --- | --- | --- |  \n| examples  | 14766  | 1866  | 1764  |  \n| documents  | 2461  | 311  | 294  |  \nCopy to bucket new\nUse this dataset \n\nDownloads last month\n    136\nNumber of rows: 22,803 Total file size: 2.23 GB\nSystem theme\nCompany\nTOS⟨55⟩ Privacy⟨56⟩ About⟨57⟩ Careers⟨58⟩ ⟨1⟩\nWebsite\nModels⟨2⟩ Datasets⟨3⟩ Spaces⟨4⟩ Pricing⟨8⟩ Docs⟨6⟩\n",
